101 + 989899)(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nNext, compute the values inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n1001001 - 1001 = 1000000\n\\]\n\n\\[\n1010101 + 989899 = 2000000\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2000000 \\times 1000000 = 2 \\times 10^{12}\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(2 \\times 10^{12}\\) has the rightmost non-zero digit \\(2\\) and it is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes.\n\nTherefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(2, 12)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the given problem, we will first simplify the expression given:\n\n\\[\n(1001001)(1010101) + (989899)(1001001) - (1001)(989899) - (1010101)(1001)\n\\]\n\nWe will start by factoring the expression.\n\nNotice that:\n\n\\[\n(1001001)(1010101) - (1010101)(1001) = 1010101(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nSimilarly,\n\n\\[\n(989899)(1001001) - (1001)(989899) = 989899(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies our original expression to:\n\n\\[\n1010101(1001001 - 1001) + 989899(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nNow, we factor out the common term \\( (1001001 - 1001) \\):\n\n\\[\n(1010101 + 989899)(1001001 - 1001)\n\\]\n\nNext, compute the values inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n1001001 - 1001 = 1000000\n\\]\n\n\\[\n1010101 + 989899 = 2000000\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n2000000 \\times 1000000 = 2 \\times 10^{12}\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(2 \\times 10^{12}\\) has the rightmost non-zero digit \\(2\\) and it is followed by \\(12\\) zeroes.\n\nTherefore, the ordered pair \\((a, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(2, 12)}\n\\]","id":"algebra:117"}
